License: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception (LICENSE, copied from the tarball root).
Why vendored: REWRITE_PLAN.md D13 (plug-in runtime replacing wasmi) and D17 (not packaged widely).

How the files were selected: exactly the sources WAMR's CMake (build-scripts/runtime_lib.cmake)
compiles for an interpreter-only build (WAMR_BUILD_INTERP=1, WAMR_BUILD_FAST_INTERP=1, no AOT/JIT,
no libc-builtin/WASI, WAMR_BUILD_INVOKE_NATIVE_GENERAL=1 instead of the per-CPU assembly, the
thread manager for wasm_runtime_terminate) on POSIX: core/iwasm/common/*.c (+ arch/
invokeNative_general.c), core/iwasm/interpreter/{wasm_loader,wasm_runtime,wasm_interp_fast}.c,
core/iwasm/libraries/thread-mgr, core/shared/utils/*.c, core/shared/mem-alloc (ems), the POSIX
platform files the platform cmake keeps without WASI (posix_{malloc,memmap,sleep,thread,time,
blocking_op}.c, plus common/memory/mremap.c where mremap is missing) for linux, darwin and
freebsd, and every header those include (core/config.h, core/version.h, core/iwasm/include/*.h
used, aot/aot_runtime.h and compilation/aot.h which common code includes unconditionally).
Nothing else from the tarball (no samples, tests, product-mini, language bindings, AOT, JIT,
libraries, WASI). The configuration (-D flags) lives in the Makefile (WAMR_CPPFLAGS).

Local changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b); each is marked "PhotoCraft local change" in the file):
  core/iwasm/interpreter/wasm_loader.c, destroy_const_expr_stack(): skip stack entries whose
  `expr` is NULL. With WASM_ENABLE_EXTENDED_CONST_EXPR, plain constants are pushed with
  expr == NULL, so a malformed constant expression (e.g. a data segment offset of the wrong type)
  dereferenced NULL while cleaning up: found by tests/plugins/test_abi.c (byte-flipped modules).

